The page sent with 408 Request Timeout said "No request appeared within
60 seconds", but the request headers are timed out after
HEADER_READ_TIMEOUT, which is 30 seconds. Build the text from
HEADER_READ_TIMEOUT so that it states the actual limit and stays in step
with it.

---
 networking/httpd.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/networking/httpd.c
+++ b/networking/httpd.c
@@ -480,7 +480,7 @@
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_HTTPD_ETAG
 	{ "Not Modified" },
 #endif
-	{ "Request Timeout", "No request appeared within 60 seconds" },
+	{ "Request Timeout", "No request appeared within "STR(HEADER_READ_TIMEOUT)" seconds" },
 	{ "Not Implemented", "The requested method is not recognized" },
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_HTTPD_BASIC_AUTH
 	{ "Unauthorized", "" },
